      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, it definitely hits the professional notes. \n\nThe thing is, the client is a bit nervous about how this will land. They're worried it might come across a bit too \"corporate\" or dry, and that it won't really turn the mood around for the guest. I just checked the draft against our sentiment tool, and the positivity score was a bit lower than I'd like to see for a 'reputation recovery' task.\n\nI'm not telling you to go overboard or be fake—I know that's a disaster—but can we try a version that feels a bit more warm and encouraging? Maybe lean into a more positive and welcoming tone while still being real about the mistake? I want to see if we can bump that positivity metric up a little without losing the sincerity.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
